 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. Who are you? Nice of you. They'd probably appreciate small thoughtful things rather than anything at all, though. Did they play themselves, or teach someone who did? So sad. Doorbells last much longer than we do. It' usually outside, on the wall near the meter. Turn it with your wrist watch in reach. A few revolutions at least. You' want to check it every now and then, since readings jump around bit. With a card, you can track the actual fuel used, which you can see immediately with a meter reading only every few months. With a verifiable meter reading, you can also show any significant drop in usage over time was the heating",
